node_modules/
__pycache__/
report.json
*.pyc
*.log

# Store directories a subject creates relative to its working directory. They appear in the repo
# root whenever a probe runs from here rather than from a temp directory, and they are evidence, not
# source.
.memdb/
.retained/
.venv-bm/

# Generated by "python check.py --badge". A subject's badge belongs to the subject's repository, not
# to this one.
conformance-badge.svg

# The stores durability.py fills and then damages. results/durability.json is the record of what
# happened; these directories are the debris, and a repository that committed them would be
# committing eleven half-written databases to make a point.
results/durability/
